nodes.body:
@yichiche Body updated and the line breaks are fixed.

One change you should know about, since it changes the opening you asked for: this PR no longer has an FFN path. Measuring on current `main` showed the FFN-side quantized read never engaged on Qwen3-Next's default configuration. Shared-expert fusion is on, so there is no separate FP8 shared expert to feed, and aiter's tuned Qwen3-Next MoE config already quantizes activations inside the MoE kernel. Instrumenting a running server showed the FFN read plain at all 192 sites, and removing it measured within ±0.5% at every concurrency with GSM8K unchanged. So it's gone, and with it every change to `layer_boundary`: this PR is now `layernorm.py`, `parallel_state.py` and one test file, +290/−1.

The opening now states what the PR changes on gfx950 rather than the FFN gap, which no longer applies. The merge with `main` (`d64ee5ab`) is pushed as well, for the rebase gate.

